<title>INDIA: TABLE-India's HDFC Q1 97/98 net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-India's HDFC Q1 97/98 net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		    549.08 vs    427.26</p>
<p>    Income from operations  3,316.63 vs  2,645.83</p>
<p>    Other income		    2.33 vs	1.87</p>
<p>    Interest expense	  2,374.79 vs  1,871.78</p>
<p>    Other expenses		164.58 vs    140.09</p>
<p>    Depreciation		   97.5  vs     95.0</p>
<p>    Tax			     133.0  vs    113.57</p>
<p>Note: Housing Development Finance Corporation (HDFC) is India's leading housing finance firm. It said loan sanctions in the first quarter of 1997/98 (April-March) were 5.19 billion rupees against 4.14 billion in the corresponding period last year. Disbursals during the period rose to 3.38 billion rupees from 2.75 billion in the year-ago period, the firm said in a statement. The results were unaudited, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
